e target letter-sound combinations /ɪə/, /θ/, /ð/, digraph wh and tw from an oral text\npronounce words with the target letter-sound combinations /ɪə/, /θ/, /ð/, digraph wh, and tw in preparation for reading\nuse words related to the theme in relevant contexts\nrespond to simple specific two-directional instructions in oral communication\nrecognise the target letter - sound combinations nd, nk, / eɪ/ / əʊ/ and / aɪ/ in given words\npronounce words with the target letter-sound combinations nd, nk, / eɪ/ / əʊ/ and / aɪ/ in preparation for reading\nuse new words related to the theme in relevant contexts\nrespond appropriately to simple specific two- directional instructions in oral communication\nrealise the importance of pronouncing and using vocabulary correctly for effective communication\nrecognise words with the target letter-sound combinations ‘br’, /ə/, /iː /, / eɪ/ and / əʊ/ in preparation for reading\npronounce new words correctly for clarity in speech\nrespond to simple specific two- directional instructions in oral communication\nrecognise words with the target letter-sound combinations cr, /ɜː/, /eɪ/ /aɪ/, words ending with the letter ‘y’ pronounced as /i/, and / ə / as in words ending with ar correctly\npronounce words with the target letter-sound combinations cr, /ɜː/, /eɪ/, /aɪ/, /i/ and / ə / as in words ending with ar in preparation for reading\nlisten to simple specific two- directional instructions in oral communication\nrecognise words with the target letter-sound combinations /ɪə/, / ə /, /ɜː/, /dr /, /ɔɪ/ and /aɪ / in a text\npronounce words with the target letter-sound combinations /ɪə/, / ə /, /ɜː/, /dr /, /ɔɪ/ and /aɪ in preparation for reading\nuse new words in relevant contexts to talk about position and direction\nappreciate the importance of listening attentively for effective communication\nidentify the target letter-sound combinations ‘fr’ /aʊ/, / ɔː/ and /ə/ during a conversation about the environment\narticulate words with the target le