(5305, 44, 8, 100, 'Arabic', 100, 808, 3073, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Arabic: Writing - Guided Writing (2 sessions)', 'Writing', 22, 'Writing', 'Guided Writing (2 sessions)', 'list weather features for comprehension\nuse basic descriptive words to write simple sentences based on the theme\nappreciate the skill of writing for effective communication', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:55', '2026-08-01 00:02:55'),
(5306, 44, 8, 100, 'Arabic', 100, 808, 3074, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Arabic: Writing - Guided Writing: Paragraph Writing (2 sessions)', 'Writing', 23, 'Writing', 'Guided Writing: Paragraph Writing (2 sessions)', 'construct simple sentences to express ideas related to the theme\ncreate a coherent paragraph for comprehension\ndevelop positive attitude towards writing Arabic', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:55', '2026-08-01 00:02:55'),
(5307, 44, 8, 98, 'Creative Arts', 98, 793, 2973, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Creative Arts: Creating and Executing - Percussion Musical Instruments (Drawing)', 'Creating and Executing', 1, 'Creating and Executing', 'Percussion Musical Instruments (Drawing)', 'identify indigenous percussion musical instruments from different Kenyan communities\nclassify indigenous Kenyan percussion musical instruments, as melodic or non-melodic\ndiscuss the function(\nof parts of a percussion musical instrument\nimprovise rhythmic patterns using indigenous percussion musical instruments\nmake charcoal sticks for drawing\ncreate tonal value on a drawing of a percussion\nin sound production, • practice improvising rhythmic patterns to accompany songs using percussion instruments, • talk about value/ tone as an element of art created on virtual and actual sample pictures, • collaboratively, collect materials and tools to make charcoal 1. What is the importance of percussion instruments from different communities in Kenya? 2. How is tonal variation created in a drawing? 2 instrument using the smudging technique\nappreciate indigenous percussion instruments from Kenyan communities and pictures drawn. sticks following the correct procedure while observing safety, • use charcoal sticks to illustrate how to create tone/value by smudging technique, • draw using charcoal sticks a picture of one percussion instrument and create tonal variation by smudging technique, • show and talk about own and peers’ percussion instruments and drawings in a just and fair manner', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:55', '2026-08-01 00:02:55'),
(5308, 44, 8, 98, 'Creative Arts', 98, 793, 2974, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Creative Arts: Creating and Executing - Netball', 'Creating and Executing', 2, 'Creating and Executing', 'Netball', 'discuss the skills of passing and catching in Netball\nmake a ball using macramé technique\nperform the skills of passing, and catching in Netball\nappreciate Netball as a team game for enjoyment', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:55', '2026-08-01 00:02:55'),
(5309, 44, 8, 98, 'Creative Arts', 98, 793, 2975, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Creative Arts: Creating and Executing - Painting and Montage', 'Creating and Executing', 3, 'Creating and Executing', 'Painting and Montage', 'classify colours into primary and secondary for painting\npaint a picture for colour value application\ncreate a montage composition for expression\nappreciate painting and montage as methods of making pictures', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:55', '2026-08-01 00:02:55'),
(5310, 44, 8, 98, 'Creative Arts', 98, 793, 2976, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Creative Arts: Creating and Executing - Rhythm', 'Creating and Executing', 4, 'Creating and Executing', 'Rhythm', 'interpret rhythmic patterns involving the crotchet, pair of quaver and their rests\nwrite the French rhythm taa and ta-te, names using free hand lettering\ndescribe the qualities of a good rhythmic pattern\ncompose a rhythmic pattern involving a crochet, a pair of quavers and their rests\nenjoy creating rhythmic patterns', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:55', '2026-08-01 00:02:55'),
(5311, 44, 8, 98, 'Creative Arts', 98, 793, 2977, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Creative Arts: Creating and Executing - Melody', 'Creating and Executing', 5, 'Creating and Executing', 'Melody', 'identify sol-fa syllables d r m in a simple melody\ninterpret hand signs for the sol-fa syllables d r m for pitch discrimination\nstate the qualities of a good melody as a foundation to composition\ncreate short melodies using the sol-fa syllables d, r and m\nmodel clay slabs with sol-fa syllables using coil and slab techniques\nas sounded on a melodic instrument/voice, • watch videos/demonstrations of execution of the Kodaly hand signs for the sol-fa syllables d, r m and practise performing the hand signs, • brainstorm on the qualities of a good melody, • apply composition techniques to create short melodies based on the sol-fa syllables d r m and the note symbols; crotchet, a pair of quavers and their rests, • collect clay for modelling from the local environment, How can interesting melodies be created? 12\nenjoy creating short melodies and modelling using clay. • roll clay into slab and cut out three rectangular pieces of three different sizes, • model so-lfa syllables (d r\nusing coil technique and attach on the slabs', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:55', '2026-08-01 00:02:55'),
(5312, 44, 8, 98, 'Creative Arts', 98, 794, 2978, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Creative Arts: Performing and Displaying - Athletics', 'Performing and Displaying', 6, 'Performing and Displaying', 'Athletics', 'discuss the sprint starts and sprinting techniques in athletics\nperform the sprint starts and sprinting techniques for skill development\npaint the Kenyan flag for an athletic event\nrecognise the value of flying the Kenyan flag during an athletics event', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:55', '2026-08-01 00:02:55'),
(5313, 44, 8, 98, 'Creative Arts', 98, 794, 2979, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Creative Arts: Performing and Displaying - Gymnastics', 'Performing and Displaying', 7, 'Performing and Displaying', 'Gymnastics', 'explain a crab balance and a side roll in gymnastics\nperform the crab balance for skill acquisition\nexecute the side roll for skill acquisition\nappreciate performing gymnastics skills for enjoyment', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:55', '2026-08-01 00:02:55'),
(5314, 44, 8, 98, 'Creative Arts', 98, 794, 2980, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Creative Arts: Performing and Displaying - Songs', 'Performing and Displaying', 8, 'Performing and Displaying', 'Songs', 'sing different types of songs applying performance techniques\nperform the East African Community Anthem in unison\nidentify types of folk songs performed by indigenous Kenyan communities\nperform an indigenous Kenyan folk song applying performance techniques\nvalue performing indigenous songs from different Kenyan communities', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:55', '2026-08-01 00:02:55'),
(5315, 44, 8, 98, 'Creative Arts', 98, 794, 2981, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Creative Arts: Performing and Displaying - Photography', 'Performing and Displaying', 9, 'Performing and Displaying', 'Photography', 'identify digital devices for photography\ndiscuss elements of photography for familiarisation\ntake photographs using digital devices\nenjoy taking photographs using digital devices', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:55', '2026-08-01 00:02:55'),
(5316, 44, 8, 98, 'Creative Arts', 98, 794, 2982, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Creative Arts: Performing and Displaying - Descant Recorder', 'Performing and Displaying', 10, 'Performing and Displaying', 'Descant Recorder', 'identify the parts of a descant recorder for familiarisation\ncare for a descant recorder for longevity\nplay notes B, A and G using appropriate recorder techniques\nplay simple melodies based on notes B, A and G\nenjoy playing melodies using the descant recorder', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:55', '2026-08-01 00:02:55'),
(5317, 44, 8, 98, 'Creative Arts', 98, 794, 2983, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Creative Arts: Performing and Displaying - Swimming (Optional)', 'Performing and Displaying', 11, 'Performing and Displaying', 'Swimming (Optional)', 'recognise ways of water entry in the swimming pool\nplay water games in the swimming pool for fun\nfloat in water for skill acquisition\nglide in water for water confidence\nappreciate safety in and out of the swimming pool while playing water games', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:55', '2026-08-01 00:02:55'),
(5318, 44, 8, 98, 'Creative Arts', 98, 794, 2984, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Creative Arts: Performing and Displaying - Indigenous Kenyan Games (Optional)', 'Performing and Displaying', 12, 'Performing and Displaying', 'Indigenous Kenyan Games (Optional)', 'identify types of indigenous animal games played in Kenya\nperform different indigenous animal games for skill acquisition\nperform indigenous animal games to a musical rhythm for enjoyment\nappreciate the role played by animal games for fitness and health', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:55', '2026-08-01 00:02:55'),
