(5968, 44, 10, 104, 'Religious Education', 104, 915, 3624, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Religious Education: Christian Living - Alcohol, Drugs and Substance use (CRE)', 'Christian Living', 19, 'Christian Living', 'Alcohol, Drugs and Substance use', 'identify drugs commonly abused by youths in Kenya today\ndiscuss reasons why young people abuse drugs today\nexplore the effects of alcohol, drugs and substance abuse on an individual and the family\nread the scriptures provided on the effects of alcohol, drug and substance abuse\nrecommend values and life skills needed to stay free from alcohol, drug and substance abuse\nutilise values and life- skills acquired to live an alcohol, drug and substance-free life', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:58', '2026-08-01 00:02:58'),
(5969, 44, 10, 104, 'Religious Education', 104, 916, 3625, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Religious Education: Qur’an - Ulumul Qur’an (IRE)', 'Qur’an', 20, 'Qur’an', 'Ulumul Qur’an', 'state the reasons for the revelation of the Qur’an as a guide to mankind\ndescribe the stages of the revelation of the Qur’an as a sign of mercy to mankind\nnarrate the incident of the first revelation of the Qur’an at Cave Hira to show the importance of seeking knowledge\nexplain the reasons for the revelation of the Qur’an in portions for ease of its implementation\nassess the importance of the Qur’an in the day-to-day life of a Muslim as a divine guidance for humanity\nvalue the Qur’an as a book of guidance to mankind', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:58', '2026-08-01 00:02:58'),
(5970, 44, 10, 104, 'Religious Education', 104, 916, 3626, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Religious Education: Qur’an - Selected Chapters (Surah) (IRE)', 'Qur’an', 21, 'Qur’an', 'Selected Chapters (Surah)', 'read surah Ad-Dhuha (Q.93:1-11) and surah Al-Balad (Q. 90:1-20) correctly for spiritual nourishment\nexplain the meaning of surah Ad- Dhuha (Q.93:1-11) and surah Al- Balad (Q. 90:1-20) for better understanding\ndeduce the lessons of surah Ad- Dhuha (Q.93: 1-11) and surah Al- Balad (Q. 90:1-20) for application in daily life\napply the teachings of surah Ad- Dhuha (Q.93: 1-11) and surah Al- Balad (Q. 90:1-20) in their daily life to earn rewards from Allah\nappreciate the teachings of surah Ad- Dhuha (Q.93: 1-11) and surah Al- Balad (Q. 90:1-20) as a guide in daily life', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:58', '2026-08-01 00:02:58'),
(5971, 44, 10, 104, 'Religious Education', 104, 917, 3627, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Religious Education: Hadith - Ulumul Hadith (IRE)', 'Hadith', 22, 'Hadith', 'Ulumul Hadith', 'explain the meaning of hadith for better understanding\ndescribe the forms of Hadith for a better understanding of the science of Hadith (Qaul, Fiil, Taqrir, Sifat)\nstate the components of Hadith for a better understanding of the science of Hadith\nexplain the types of Hadith (Hadith Qudsy and Nabawy) as the second source of Sharia\nassess the importance of Hadith for spiritual nourishment\nemulate the life of the Prophet (S.A.W.) to earn Allah’s rewards and enhance the competency of self-efficacy\nacknowledge Hadith as a primary source of Sharia', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:58', '2026-08-01 00:02:58'),
(5972, 44, 10, 104, 'Religious Education', 104, 917, 3628, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Religious Education: Hadith - Selected Hadith (IRE)', 'Hadith', 23, 'Hadith', 'Selected Hadith', 'deduce the lessons learnt from the selected Hadith for character building\nassess the relevance of the selected Hadith in the life of a Muslim\npractise the teachings from the selected hadith in daily life\nappreciate Hadith as the second source of Islamic law and spiritual guidance', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:58', '2026-08-01 00:02:58'),
(5973, 44, 10, 104, 'Religious Education', 104, 918, 3629, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Religious Education: Pillars of Iman - Significance of Tawhid (IRE)', 'Pillars of Iman', 24, 'Pillars of Iman', 'Significance of Tawhid', 'assess the significance of Tawhid for spiritual nourishment\ndemonstrate belief in Tawhid\nappreciate Tawhid as the basis of the Islamic faith', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:58', '2026-08-01 00:02:58'),
(5974, 44, 10, 104, 'Religious Education', 104, 918, 3630, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Religious Education: Pillars of Iman - Shirk (IRE)', 'Pillars of Iman', 25, 'Pillars of Iman', 'Shirk', 'explain different types of shirk to avoid associating Allah with other beings\ndescribe different ways through which shirk is manifested to protect one’s Iman\nexamine the effects of shirk to safeguard one’s Iman\npractise acts that are devoid of shirk in daily life\nrecognise the belief in One God as the foundation of Iman', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:58', '2026-08-01 00:02:58'),
(5975, 44, 10, 104, 'Religious Education', 104, 919, 3631, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Religious Education: Devotional Acts - Swalah (IRE)', 'Devotional Acts', 26, 'Devotional Acts', 'Swalah', 'describe how congregational prayers and sunnah prayers are performed to earn rewards (Tahajud, Tahiyatul Masjid and Dhuha)\ndescribe the performance of prayers on special occasions to earn Allah (S.W.T.)’s blessing (Swalatul Janaza, Musafir,Kusuf, and Khusuf)\nperform congregational prayers, sunnah prayers and prayers on special occasions for spiritual nourishment\nassess the importance of performing congregational prayers, Sunnah prayers, and prayers on special occasions to earn rewards from Allah', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:58', '2026-08-01 00:02:58'),
(5976, 44, 10, 104, 'Religious Education', 104, 919, 3632, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Religious Education: Devotional Acts - Zakat (IRE)', 'Devotional Acts', 27, 'Devotional Acts', 'Zakat', 'describe Zakatul Maal and Zakatul Fitr as an obligation on a Muslim\ndifferentiate between Zakatul Maal and Zakatul Fitr as acts of ibadah\nidentify items exempted from Zakat payment\nassess the significance of Zakatul Maal and Zakatul Fitr to the society\nappreciate the role of zakat in the development of a Muslim society', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:58', '2026-08-01 00:02:58'),
(5977, 44, 10, 104, 'Religious Education', 104, 919, 3633, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Religious Education: Devotional Acts - Saum (IRE)', 'Devotional Acts', 28, 'Devotional Acts', 'Saum', 'describe types of Saum for ease of observance\nassess the significance of Saum for spiritual growth\nobserve saum to earn rewards from Allah\nappreciate the observance of Saum as a way of earning taqwa', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:58', '2026-08-01 00:02:58'),
(5978, 44, 10, 104, 'Religious Education', 104, 920, 3634, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Religious Education: Akhlaq (Moral Teachings) - Dimensions of Morality in Islam (IRE)', 'Akhlaq (Moral Teachings)', 29, 'Akhlaq (Moral Teachings)', 'Dimensions of Morality in Islam', 'identify sources of morality in Islam as a guide to good behaviour\nexplain the purpose of morality in promoting uprightness in the society\npractise Islamic moral values in day-to-day life to earn rewards from Allah\nregard Islamic values as a form of ibadah', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:58', '2026-08-01 00:02:58'),
(5979, 44, 10, 104, 'Religious Education', 104, 920, 3635, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Religious Education: Akhlaq (Moral Teachings) - Virtues in Islam (IRE)', 'Akhlaq (Moral Teachings)', 30, 'Akhlaq (Moral Teachings)', 'Virtues in Islam', 'explain Islamic teachings on truthfulness and forgiveness for moral growth\nassess the significance of upholding truthfulness and forgiveness for harmonious co-existence in the society\nexercise truthfulness and forgiveness in day-to-day life to earn rewards from Allah (S.W.T.)\nappreciate Islamic virtues for a morally upright society', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:58', '2026-08-01 00:02:58'),
(5980, 44, 10, 104, 'Religious Education', 104, 920, 3636, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Religious Education: Akhlaq (Moral Teachings) - Prohibitions in Islam (IRE)', 'Akhlaq (Moral Teachings)', 31, 'Akhlaq (Moral Teachings)', 'Prohibitions in Islam', 'describe the effects of drug abuse for healthy living\nexamine the rationale behind the prohibition of drugs as a way of fostering positive character formation\nexplain remedies for drug abuse for a healthy and morally upright society\nabstain from abusing drugs to earn Allah’s pleasure\nacknowledge the rationale for the prohibition of drugs for the growth and development of the nation', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:58', '2026-08-01 00:02:58'),
(5981, 44, 10, 104, 'Religious Education', 104, 921, 3637, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Religious Education: Muamalat (Social Relationship) - Marriage (IRE)', 'Muamalat (Social Relationship)', 32, 'Muamalat (Social Relationship)', 'Marriage', 'explain the purpose of marriage as a means of fulfilling one’s faith\nstate the conditions for a valid marriage in Islam\ndescribe the rights and responsibilities in marriage for observance of Allah (S.W.T.)’s commandments\nregard marriage as a way of validating the establishment of a family', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:58', '2026-08-01 00:02:58'),
(5982, 44, 10, 104, 'Religious Education', 104, 921, 3638, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Religious Education: Muamalat (Social Relationship) - Trade and Finance in Islam (IRE)', 'Muamalat (Social Relationship)', 33, 'Muamalat (Social Relationship)', 'Trade and Finance in Islam', 'identify the halal and haram sources of earning for legitimate livelihood\ndescribe the legitimate ways of spending income to earn Allah (S.W.T.)’s Pleasure\nanalyse the effects of spending income in haram ways in the life of a Muslim\nexplain the importance of lawful earnings as an act of ibadah\nassess the benefits of spending income in legitimate ways to earn rewards from Allah (S.W.T.)\napply the knowledge of the halal way of earning in daily life\nappreciate halal sources of earning and spending as a fulfilment of Allah (S.W.T.)’s command', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:58', '2026-08-01 00:02:58'),
(5983, 44, 10, 104, 'Religious Education', 104, 921, 3639, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Religious Education: Muamalat (Social Relationship) - Contemporary issues (IRE)', 'Muamalat (Social Relationship)', 34, 'Muamalat (Social Relationship)', 'Contemporary issues', 'identify the rights of women in Islam for gender parity\ndescribe the modes of transmission of HIV/ and AIDS and COVID-19 to avoid transmission\nillustrate safe behaviors while using the road for safe road use\nexplain the possible remedies for the spread of HIV/ and AIDS and COVID-19 for healthy living\nhonour the rights of women as a fulfilment of the teachings of the Prophet (S.A.W.)', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:58', '2026-08-01 00:02:58'),
(5984, 44, 10, 104, 'Religious Education', 104, 922, 3640, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Religious Education: Islamic Heritage and Civilisation - Reforms introduced by Prophet Muhammad (S.A.W.) (IRE)', 'Islamic Heritage and Civilisation', 35, 'Islamic Heritage and Civilisation', 'Reforms introduced by Prophet Muhammad (S.A.W.)', 'describe the socio- religious, political, and economic reforms introduced by Prophet Muhammad (S.A.W.) as an agent of change\nassess the importance of the socio-religious, political, and economic reforms introduced by Prophet Muhammad (S.A.W.) to the world civilisation\napply lessons learnt from the reforms introduced by Prophet Muhammad (S.A.W.)\ntreasure the reforms introduced by Prophet Muhammad (S.A.W.) for a morally upright society', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:58', '2026-08-01 00:02:58');
INSERT IGNORE INTO `schemes_of_work` (`id`, `teacher_id`, `class_id`, `subject_id`, `subject_name`, `learning_area_id`, `strand_id`, `sub_strand_id`, `coverage_id`, `academic_year_id`, `term_id`, `term_number`, `title`, `description`, `week_number`, `strand`, `sub_strand`, `learning_outcomes`, `key_vocabulary`, `resources`, `activities`, `assessment_methods`, `status`, `approved_by`, `approved_at`, `rejection_reason`, `file_path`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(5985, 44, 10, 105, 'Social Studies', 105, 923, 3641, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Social Studies: Social Studies - Career and Entrepreneurial Opportunities in Social Studies', 'Social Studies', 1, 'Social Studies', 'Career and Entrepreneurial Opportunities in Social Studies', 'analyze importance of social studies for personal development and service to humanity\nexplore career opportunities related to social studies in Kenya and globally\nexamine entrepreneurial opportunities for Social Studies in society\napply appropriate strategies for addressing gender stereotypes associated with career choices and entrepreneurial opportunities in Social Studies\ndemonstrate respect for one’s gender identity in pursuit of Social Studies careers and entrepreneurial opportunities\nappreciate the role of social studies for promotion of social cohesion • brainstorm on entrepreneurial opportunities for Social Studies in society • create a poster of all entrepreneurial opportunities for Social Studies in society and display it in school entrepreneurial opportunities in Social Studies?', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:58', '2026-08-01 00:02:58'),
(5986, 44, 10, 105, 'Social Studies', 105, 924, 3642, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Social Studies: Natural and the Built Environments in Africa - Maps and Map Work', 'Natural and the Built Environments in Africa', 2, 'Natural and the Built Environments in Africa', 'Maps and Map Work', 'describe the position, shape and size of Africa\nIdentify the countries that make up the African continent\nuse latitudes and longitudes to locate places and features on a map\ncalculate the time of different places in the world using longitudes\ndistinguish pictures, plans and maps as used in social studies\nrecognize the importance of maps in day to day lives as used in social studies. • research on the three types of maps used in Social Studies and make summary notes (Topographical maps, Sketch maps and Atlas Maps) • discuss in groups the uses of different types of maps and present in class', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:58', '2026-08-01 00:02:58'),
(5987, 44, 10, 105, 'Social Studies', 105, 924, 3643, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Social Studies: Natural and the Built Environments in Africa - The Earth and the Solar system', 'Natural and the Built Environments in Africa', 3, 'Natural and the Built Environments in Africa', 'The Earth and the Solar system', 'describe the origin, size, shape and position of the earth in the solar system\nexamine the effects of rotation and revolution of the earth on human activities\nillustrate the internal structure of the earth in the solar system', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:58', '2026-08-01 00:02:58'),
(5988, 44, 10, 105, 'Social Studies', 105, 924, 3644, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Social Studies: Natural and the Built Environments in Africa - Weather', 'Natural and the Built Environments in Africa', 4, 'Natural and the Built Environments in Africa', 'Weather', 'describe the elements of weather in the environment\nanalyse and interpret data on weather conditions in the environment\nexplain the factors considered when siting a weather station\nconstruct selected instruments for measuring elements of weather\nexamine the significance of weather to human environment', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:58', '2026-08-01 00:02:58'),
(5989, 44, 10, 105, 'Social Studies', 105, 924, 3645, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Social Studies: Natural and the Built Environments in Africa - Historical Information', 'Natural and the Built Environments in Africa', 5, 'Natural and the Built Environments in Africa', 'Historical Information', 'identify various sources of historical information in the society\ndistinguish between primary and secondary sources of historical information\nexplore how various sources of historical information have been preserved over the years\nassess the significance of various sources of historical information in providing evidence of past human accounts\nrecognize sources of historical information in understanding past human accounts', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:58', '2026-08-01 00:02:58'),
(5990, 44, 10, 105, 'Social Studies', 105, 925, 3646, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Social Studies: People and Population - Human Origin', 'People and Population', 6, 'People and Population', 'Human Origin', 'explore the traditional stories of human origin from the selected African communities\nexplain the religious stories about the origin of humankind\nexamine factors proving that Africa is the cradle of humankind\nrecord traditional stories about the origin of humankind in society', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:58', '2026-08-01 00:02:58'),
(5991, 44, 10, 105, 'Social Studies', 105, 925, 3647, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Social Studies: People and Population - Early Civilizatio n', 'People and Population', 7, 'People and Population', 'Early Civilizatio n', 'define the term kngdom as used in history\nexplore factors that led to growth of the selected ancient Kingdoms in Africa\nlocate the selected ancient kingdoms on a map of Africa\nassess the contributions of early African civilization to the modern world\nappreciate the contribution of early civilization to the development of modern world', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:58', '2026-08-01 00:02:58'),
(5992, 44, 10, 105, 'Social Studies', 105, 925, 3648, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Social Studies: People and Population - Social Organization of selected African Communities up to', 'People and Population', 8, 'People and Population', 'Social Organization of selected African Communities up to', 'locate on a map of Africa the areas settled by the selected African communities\ndescribe the social organization of selected African communities up to 1900\ncompare the social organization of the selected African communities up to 1900\nValue the Kenyan and African rich cultural diversity among communities\ndesire to appreciate and promote positive interactions among', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:58', '2026-08-01 00:02:58'),
(5993, 44, 10, 105, 'Social Studies', 105, 925, 3649, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Social Studies: People and Population - Human Diversity and inclusion', 'People and Population', 9, 'People and Population', 'Human Diversity and inclusion', 'identify personality attributes which make individuals different from others\ncategorize desirable and undesirable personality attributes in a multi- cultural society\ninvestigate different components of human identity in a multicultural society\napply inclusion in day to day interactions\nshow respect to others to promote social cohesion', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:58', '2026-08-01 00:02:58'),
(5994, 44, 10, 105, 'Social Studies', 105, 925, 3650, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Social Studies: People and Population - Slavery and Servitude', 'People and Population', 10, 'People and Population', 'Slavery and Servitude', 'identify the various forms of slavery and servitude in traditional African society\ndiscuss the factors that led to development of the Indian Ocean slave trade\ndescribe the organization of Indian Ocean slave trade in 15th Century\noutline the various social injustices committed on the Africans during Indian Ocean slave trade in 15th Century slave trade\nIllustrate the geographical extent of the regions covered by Indian Ocean slave trade in Africa', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:58', '2026-08-01 00:02:58'),
(5995, 44, 10, 105, 'Social Studies', 105, 925, 3651, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Social Studies: People and Population - Population Distribution in Africa', 'People and Population', 11, 'People and Population', 'Population Distribution in Africa', 'explain factors influencing population distribution in Africa\nlocate densely and sparsely populated areas on a map of Africa\nillustrate settlement patterns in Africa using diagrams\nappreciate patterns of population settlement in Africa', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:58', '2026-08-01 00:02:58'),
(5996, 44, 10, 105, 'Social Studies', 105, 925, 3652, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Social Studies: People and Population - Field Work', 'People and Population', 12, 'People and Population', 'Field Work', 'identify types of field work in Social Studies\nanalyse methods of data collection and recording in fieldwork\nexamine methods of data analysis and presentation in field work\nexplore challenges and solutions in carrying out field work\napply procedures of carrying out fieldwork in research', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:58', '2026-08-01 00:02:58'),
(5997, 44, 10, 105, 'Social Studies', 105, 926, 3653, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Social Studies: Resources and Economic Activities - Agriculture', 'Resources and Economic Activities', 13, 'Resources and Economic Activities', 'Agriculture', 'locate areas where early agriculture was practiced in selected geographical regions\nexplore crops grown and animals kept in selected regions during early agriculture\nillustrate methods of irrigation used in ancient Egypt\nassess the contribution of the Nile valley agriculture to world civilization\nValue the importance of domestication of plant and animals in Africa\ndevelop desire to practice agriculture as an economic activity', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:58', '2026-08-01 00:02:58'),
(5998, 44, 10, 105, 'Social Studies', 105, 926, 3654, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Social Studies: Resources and Economic Activities - Economic Organization of Selected African Communities up to', 'Resources and Economic Activities', 14, 'Resources and Economic Activities', 'Economic Organization of Selected African Communities up to', 'locate on a map of Africa areas occupied by the selected African communities\ndiscuss the economic activities practiced by the selected African communities\ncompare the economic activities of the selected African communities\nappreciate the economic activities of the selected African communities', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:58', '2026-08-01 00:02:58'),
(5999, 44, 10, 105, 'Social Studies', 105, 926, 3655, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Social Studies: Resources and Economic Activities - Internal Dynamics and Transformation in Africa', 'Resources and Economic Activities', 15, 'Resources and Economic Activities', 'Internal Dynamics and Transformation in Africa', 'explain the transformation brought by introduction of money in Africa\ndiscuss the use of money economy in trade\ncompare the use of money in currency trade and barter trade in Africa\ndevelop interest to use money wisely for economic gain', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:58', '2026-08-01 00:02:58'),
(6000, 44, 10, 105, 'Social Studies', 105, 926, 3656, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Social Studies: Resources and Economic Activities - Sustainable use of resources', 'Resources and Economic Activities', 16, 'Resources and Economic Activities', 'Sustainable use of resources', 'discuss the concept of sustainable use of resources in society\nexplore sustainable ways of using resources available in the community\napply sustainable use of resources available in the community\nappreciate sustainable use of resources for sustenance of life', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:58', '2026-08-01 00:02:58'),
(6001, 44, 10, 105, 'Social Studies', 105, 927, 3657, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Social Studies: Political Development and Governance - Political Development in Africa up to 1900’', 'Political Development and Governance', 17, 'Political Development and Governance', 'Political Development in Africa up to 1900’', 'investigate the political organization of the selected African communities up to 1900\ndiscuss the concepts “Scramble for and Partition” of Africa\nidentify the various European groups that came to Africa\nExplain factors that led to the presence of Europeans in Africa\nmatch the countries in Africa with their colonial masters\nexamine the terms of the Berlin Conference of 1884-1885 on the partitioning of Africa', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:58', '2026-08-01 00:02:58'),
(6002, 44, 10, 105, 'Social Studies', 105, 927, 3658, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Social Studies: Political Development and Governance - The Constitution of Kenya', 'Political Development and Governance', 18, 'Political Development and Governance', 'The Constitution of Kenya', 'discuss the importance of the Constitution of Kenya for mutual social wellbeing\nexplore the national values as provided in the Constitution of Kenya for promotion of good governance\nanalyze ways of upholding and protecting the Constitution of Kenya for social cohesion\ndevelop desire to uphold and protect the Constitution of Kenya for promotion of ethical and responsible citizenship', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:58', '2026-08-01 00:02:58'),
(6003, 44, 10, 105, 'Social Studies', 105, 927, 3659, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Social Studies: Political Development and Governance - Democracy', 'Political Development and Governance', 19, 'Political Development and Governance', 'Democracy', 'identify types of democracy practiced in Africa\nassess the importance of democracy in society\nexplain the role of citizens in democratic representation\nexamine the characteristics of various types of democracy in governance\napply democratic values in interactions with others in the community\ndesire to promote democratic values in', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:58', '2026-08-01 00:02:58'),
(6004, 44, 10, 105, 'Social Studies', 105, 927, 3660, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Social Studies: Political Development and Governance - Human Rights', 'Political Development and Governance', 20, 'Political Development and Governance', 'Human Rights', 'examine the evolution of human rights as practiced in society\nclassify human rights as stipulated in the human rights instruments\nexplore characteristics of human rights in society\nanalyze the concept of equity and non- discrimination in fostering solidarity\ntake action to promote equity and non- discrimination for posterity\ndemonstrate respect , adherence to and promotion of human rights for sanctity of life', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:58', '2026-08-01 00:02:58'),
(6005, 44, 10, 105, 'Social Studies', 105, 927, 3661, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Social Studies: Political Development and Governance - African Diasporas', 'Political Development and Governance', 21, 'Political Development and Governance', 'African Diasporas', 'describe the concept of “African Diasporas”\nexplore the factors that contributed to the presence of African diasporas across the world\nlocate on the world map countries inhabited by African Diasporas on the World map\nassess the role of the diasporas in the political development in Africa\nAcknowledge the African diasporas for promotion of African unity in society today', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:58', '2026-08-01 00:02:58'),
(6006, 44, 10, 105, 'Social Studies', 105, 927, 3662, NULL, NULL, 8, NULL, 'Social Studies: Political Development and Governance - Global Citizenship', 'Political Development and Governance', 22, 'Political Development and Governance', 'Global Citizenship', 'explain why there is interconnectedness and interdependence among countries in the world today\ninvestigate positive and negative effects of globalization at local and national levels\ndescribe qualities of a global citizen in the modern society\ndesire to contribute to the wellbeing of the international community while maintaining a sense of rootedness to Kenya\ndevelop a sense of belonging to a common humanity for harmonious living', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'draft', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-01 00:02:58', '2026-08-01 00:02:58'),
