ntences\nuse facial expressions, eye contact and gestures appropriately during conversations\nappreciate the role of accurate pronunciation and non-verbal cues in communication\nidentify words with the sounds /f/, /n/, / h/, / ɒ / and / ɔː/ from an oral t ext\npronounce words with the sounds /f/, / n/, / h/, / ɒ / and / ɔː/ for oral fluency\nrespond to simple one- directional instructions using new words\nappreciate th e role of accurate pronunciation in communication\nidentify words with the sounds /b/, /r/, /u/, and /g/ in a text\npronounce words with the sounds /b/, /r/, /u/, and /g/ in preparation for reading\nuse words featuring the target sounds in short sentences\nacknowledge the role of accurate pronunciation in oral communication\nidentify the sounds /k/, /d/, and /w/ from an audio text\npronounce words with the sounds /k/, /d/, and /w/ accurately for clarity\nuse words related to the theme featuring the sounds /k/, /d/, and /w/ in relevant contexts\nvalue the role of accurate pronunciation in oral fluency\nidentify words with the sounds /k/, /j/, /l/, and /s/ from written texts\npronounce words with the sounds /k/, /j/, /l/, and /s/ for oral fluency\nuse vocabulary related to the theme in oral sentences\nvalue the role of vocabulary in communication\nidentify words with the sounds /æ/ / ɔː / /i:/ /u:/ / ɔɪ / and / eɪ / for oral fluency\npronounce words with the sounds /æ/ / ɔː / /i:/ /u:/ / ɔɪ / and / eɪ / for speech clarity\nuse words related to the theme in oral sentences\nrealise the importance of varied vocabulary in communication\npick out the sounds: / ʃ/, /tʃ/, /θ/ and /ð/ from a text\npronounce words with the sounds: / ʃ/, /tʃ/, /θ/, and /ð/ correctly for clarity of speech\nuse the vocabulary learnt in relevant contexts\nadvocate for appropriate pronunciation for clarity in communication\nstate the words with the sounds /e /, / iː/, and / eə / from an audio text\narticulate the words with the sounds /e /, / iː/, and / eə / for speech clarity\nuse v